WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.273
Read the given information
Solve the equation stating that the function's derivative equals minus twice
the function plus six. There is also a condition that its value at zero is
one.

2
00:00:15.273 --> 00:00:29.182
Find the equilibrium
Start with the constant solution. A constant has derivative zero, so minus
twice this constant plus six must be zero. The constant is three.

3
00:00:29.182 --> 00:00:43.091
Write the general solution
The general solution is three plus a constant times e to the power minus two
x. Determine this constant using the given initial condition.

4
00:00:43.091 --> 00:00:57.455
Use the condition
Substitute x equal to zero. The exponential becomes one, so three plus the
constant equals one. Subtract three from both sides to obtain minus two.

5
00:00:57.455 --> 00:01:14.091
Obtain the function
Substitute the constant into the general formula. The solution is three minus
twice e to the power minus two x. We still need to check the derivative and
the condition.

6
00:01:14.091 --> 00:01:29.818
Verify and conclude
The derivative is four times the same exponential, which also equals minus
twice the function plus six. At zero the value is one, so the solution is
correct.
